## What We Are Building

Driving the E31 smoke forward while fixing the UX/logic snags the Director hit live:
pipeline-view sub-node visibility, Polina reading full state before answering, and —
the big one — the video-generation flow is fundamentally broken (parallel-batch with no
cap + critic churn + invalidated-plan hardfail + provider out of funds), which produced a
72-job runaway storm when the Director pressed «start video» on E31.

---

## What WORKED (with evidence)

- **Pipeline-view sub-nodes expand by default** — commit `7132f3a3`, tsc 0. One-time init
  effect opens every primary with muted children on first load.
- **Per-shot Designer/Critic hidden from rail** — commit `a04f1b8d`, tsc 0. Reference
  Designer/Critic (serve episode_references) + Video Designer/Critic (serve visual_generator)
  fan out per-shot → hidden; they live in the shot kebab. Episode-level critics stay.
- **Polina reads full state before answering** — commit `4bbfd341`, tsc 0. Failure-mode-2
  rule: read getStateMatrix (shot/ref/video/music/final) AND getEpisode (stage-level incl.
  pre-production, assets_in_review); interpret assets_in_review>0 as «output exists».
- **Video storm STOPPED** — killed 72→0 active E31 video jobs (VANIM:63/VGEN:8/VPREV:1) by
  agent_id; sweeps 2&3 = 0 respawns; ref jobs (EXEC-EREF*) untouched (ref was DONE, 0 active).
  Confirmed via job-status counts + activity-event drain.
- **SH21 ref image inspected** (Read as image): location canon good; but Sandy fully cloaked
  (hourglass invisible) + the «stapler» reads as an official/robot, not a stapler.

Earlier in session (companion file, all committed in `76183dfd`): metelka+empty_bg canon
restored on Drive; Bible-canon Drive-backup guard; episode.target_runtime; storyboard v3
rewritten 35s→60s (20→27 shots, +5 false_success beats), readability PASS_WITH_UNCERTAINTY.

